t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Version Added</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">v1.25.0</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Date Added</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">July 14th, 2023</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\n\t</section>\n\n\n\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p>The <b>Small Bomb</b> has a <b>very powerful explosion</b>, but a <b>small radius</b>. Like any other explosive, it damages trees and ores, and can be used to open the gate at the <a href=\"/wiki/Skull_Rock\" title=\"Skull Rock\">Skull Rock</a> to get the <a href=\"/wiki/Skull\" title=\"Skull\">Skull</a>.\n</p><p>Unlike dynamite, bombs have a delayed chain reaction.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Trivia\">Trivia</span></h2>\n<ul><li>The Small Bomb was originally priced at $5,000 and then $3,000</li>\n<li>Most explodable walls require 2-3 Small Bombs.</li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260903112614\nCache expiry: 2592000\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.031 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 79/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 61/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 7/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 28/5000000 bytes\nLua time usage: 0.005/7.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 1019470/104857600 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   24.123      1 Template:Explosive\n100.00%   24.123      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key 1.43.9_prod_oaklands:pcache:idhash:1025-0!sseVary=RegularPage!FandomDesktop!LegacyGalleries and timestamp 20260903112614 and revision id 17351. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>","categories":["Items","Explosives","